[{:seon.task/name "no-function-does-what-ctx-can"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-11-07: less special functions, more Clojure data on the ctx atom. From an audit of ``src/my`` (a scan for writes, then reading): `my.agent/messages` looks like a read but takes, commits and empties `:inbox`: delete it, with `:fx` outcomes moved to the eval that asked. `my.task/update!`: `swap!` on `[:task ...]`, untried for `:seon.task/proofs` and `:seon.task/cause`. `my.task/fail!` writes a failure and ends the turn: data the loop reads. `my.agent/cite!` and `uncite!` work out a cite's id: try `:cites` on ctx. `my.turn/wait` ends the turn through process memory, and its docstring's fresh budget is false (docs/turn.md#the-cap). `seon.agent` isn't covered. Split before release: each gets its own proof. See docs/users.md#messages."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
